      "created_at": "2021-10-01T08:09:18Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-10-01T08:09:18Z",
      "body": "Note: I am not a lawyer, but this is my understanding of how this works.\r\n\r\n## Possible violation of GDPR, without cookie banners\r\n\r\nI see that this issue was created around the time GDPR was implemented in the EU and has not been discussed ever since. A caveat of using Google Analytics is that without _explicit user consent being requested via annoying cookie banners_ at every lesson, the Carpentries would be in _violation of GDPR._\r\n\r\n## Alternatives exist\r\n\r\nOpen source solutions (such as Matomo and Plausible) which do not track personally identifiable information would \r\n\r\n1. be better suited for an organization of such standing\r\n2. respect the user's privacy\r\n3. have possiblity to self-host\r\n4. not need cookie banners\r\n\r\n## References\r\n\r\n- https://matomo.org/cookie-consent-banners/\r\n- https://matomo.org/blog/2018/04/how-to-not-process-any-personal-data-with-matomo-and-what-it-means-for-you/\r\n- https://plausible.io/vs-matomo",
